.TH TLP\-PANEL 1 "August 2026" "tlp-panel 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tlp\-panel \- live power status and quick actions for TLP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tlp\-panel
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tlp\-panel
is a graphical panel for laptops running
.BR tlp (8).
It shows the current power draw in watts, battery charge, health and cycle
count, and the estimated runtime at the present rate.
.PP
It also changes the settings people adjust most often: the TLP profile, the
battery charge limit, the processor's maximum frequency, Wi\-Fi power saving,
runtime power management for idle devices, and AMD adaptive backlight.
.PP
Readings come from sysfs and
.IR /run/tlp ,
all readable without privileges, so the interface runs as a normal user.
Changes are applied through
.BR pkexec (1)
by the helper at
.IR /usr/libexec/tlp\-panel\-helper ,
which accepts a fixed set of verbs with validated arguments and writes only to
.IR /etc/tlp.d/90\-tlp\-panel.conf .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tlp.d/90-tlp-panel.conf
Settings written by the panel. Read by TLP after its own configuration, so
these values win.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tlp-panel/abm-supported
Whether adaptive backlight can take effect on this display.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tlp-panel/language
The interface language chosen from the main menu. Absent, or holding
.IR system ,
means follow the locale.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tlp (8),
.BR tlp-stat (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Mehmet Emrah Tunçel
